Z||000000||Eric||03-26-2001||10:09 PM||||I've got a very loud pinging noise coming from my engine between 3000 and 4500 rpm.  I checked the timing today, and it's still at 10* BTDC.  The timing was set with the computer grounded out too.  The motor is a rebuilt 2.8-3.2 with the dished hyper pistons.  I don't think they have more than a 9.0:1 compression ratio, so there should be no real problems when I run 89 octane (which I do almost exclusivly).  <P>Could this be pre-ignition?  I dumped some valvoline cleaner in it a few months ago, and I don't think it did anything either (I thought there may have been carbon deposits or something).  The heads were reworked, but they were cleaned up way smoother than stock.<P>How about the spark plugs?  I have rapidfires that were meant for a 2.8.  I'm probably way off track here, but could that cause a problem?<P>The fuel pressure is set at about 42 psi, and the air/fuel meter reads almost full rich at WOT.  There shouldn't be a lean condition causing the cylinder walls, pistons, or heads to heat up thereby inducing pre-ignition.<P>I'd like to be able to run 87 octane, but I guess I could make do with 89 if I have to.  I just don't want to shell out the extra $.20 a gallon for premium when I don't need to.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-26-2001||11:22 PM||||try 89... some of the 87's are lower than that... <P>42PSI? Are you sure that's right? sounds a tad low but I can't remember for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||03-27-2001||11:32 AM||||The engine still pings when I use 89.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||03-27-2001||12:33 PM||||Is your EGR working? <P>42PSI of FP is fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-27-2001||01:39 PM||||try the spray cleaner that you spray directly into the throttle body while its running. It may break carbon loose in your cylinders (valves and piston crowns). You will have to keep revving it to keep it running. If that doesnt stop it, try changing the timeing to 8*. Should be able to use 87 octane. Im assuming the engine is not running hot.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-27-2001||02:05 PM||||I guess it *could* be that carboned up. A can of Top Engine Cleaner would work.||||reg||1
